# Dev Server Doctor

`pnpm dev` is a supervisor (`scripts/dev-server.sh`). It frees port 4000, restarts on crash / hung `/api/health` / stale auth 404s, and kills the whole Next tree on Ctrl+C so the next start is not `EADDRINUSE`. Escape hatch: `pnpm dev:raw`. Cache wipe: `pnpm dev:restart:clean`. Probe restarts are off when `NEXT_PUBLIC_E2E=1` or `CI=1` so Playwright is not yanked mid-suite.

## Quick diagnosis (in order)

```bash
# 1. Is something listening on 4000?
ss -tlnp 2>/dev/null | grep ":4000" || echo "NOTHING ON 4000"

# 2. Is it healthy?
curl -s -o /dev/null -w "HTTP %{http_code}\n" --max-time 5 http://localhost:4000/api/health

# 3. Find the process
ps aux | grep -E "next dev|node.*next" | grep -v grep | head -3
```

## Decision tree

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| HTTP 200 on /api/health | Server healthy | Nothing to do |
| HTTP 500 on /api/health | Compilation error or env missing | Check terminal for stack trace, verify `.env.local` exists |
| ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED from Windows | WSL2 port forwarding broken | See `wsl-net-fix` skill |
| ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED from WSL too | No process on 4000 | `pnpm dev` |
| EADDRINUSE on `pnpm dev` | Stale process holds port | Kill it (commands below) |
| Server returns 500 on /en after working fine | Turbopack cache corrupted | Clear `.next/` and restart |
| First request always 500, then works | Cold compile (Turbopack) | Normal — warm it with `curl http://localhost:4000/en` once |

## Common recovery commands

```bash
# Kill anything on port 4000
fuser -k 4000/tcp 2>/dev/null || true
pkill -f "next dev" 2>/dev/null
sleep 2

# Clear Turbopack cache (only if 500s persist)
rm -rf /home/tbaltzakis/code/cloudless.gr/.next /home/tbaltzakis/code/cloudless.gr/tmp

# Verify .env.local exists with the auth vars
test -f /home/tbaltzakis/code/cloudless.gr/.env.local && \
  grep -E "^AUTH_SECRET|^AUTH_TRUST_HOST|^COGNITO_ISSUER" /home/tbaltzakis/code/cloudless.gr/.env.local || \
  echo "WARNING: .env.local missing or incomplete"

# Restart in background (user can attach via the terminal)
cd /home/tbaltzakis/code/cloudless.gr
nohup pnpm dev > /tmp/dev-server.log 2>&1 &
echo "Dev server started — logs at /tmp/dev-server.log"

# Wait for ready
for i in {1..15}; do
  code=$(curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}" --max-time 2 http://localhost:4000/api/health 2>/dev/null)
  [ "$code" = "200" ] && echo "Ready after ${i}s" && break
  sleep 1
done
```

## Recovering `.env.local` from SSM

If `.env.local` is missing, recreate it:

```bash
AUTH_SECRET=$(aws ssm get-parameter --name "/cloudless/production/AUTH_SECRET" \
  --with-decryption --output text --query Parameter.Value --region us-east-1)

# Cognito OIDC settings — read from the deployed Lambda (single source of truth)
LAMBDA_FN="cloudless-production-CloudlessSiteServerUseast1Function-ddkafukh"
read -r COGNITO_ISSUER COGNITO_CLIENT_ID COGNITO_CLIENT_SECRET COGNITO_DOMAIN < <(
  aws lambda get-function-configuration --function-name "$LAMBDA_FN" --region us-east-1 \
    --query "Environment.Variables.[COGNITO_ISSUER,COGNITO_CLIENT_ID,COGNITO_CLIENT_SECRET,COGNITO_DOMAIN]" \
    --output text)

cat > /home/tbaltzakis/code/cloudless.gr/.env.local <<EOF
COGNITO_ISSUER=${COGNITO_ISSUER}
COGNITO_CLIENT_ID=${COGNITO_CLIENT_ID}
COGNITO_CLIENT_SECRET=${COGNITO_CLIENT_SECRET}
COGNITO_DOMAIN=${COGNITO_DOMAIN}
NEXT_PUBLIC_AUTH_PROVIDER=cognito
AUTH_SECRET=${AUTH_SECRET}
AUTH_TRUST_HOST=true
AUTH_URL=http://localhost:4000
EOF
```

## Memory pressure

Turbopack can use 1–2 GB during compilation. On a 10 GB WSL2 box, running tests + dev server + Tabby + other tools at once will OOM. Check:

```bash
free -h
# If "available" < 1 GB, kill optional services:
pkill -f llama-server 2>/dev/null   # Tabby
pkill -f tabby 2>/dev/null
```

## When NOT to restart

- HMR error in browser only: just refresh the page
- One route 500s but others work: check the route file for a syntax error
- "Slow filesystem" warning: harmless, ignore
